Z||000000||fiero56||01-02-2001||12:10 AM||||What's a good paying job for a college student majoring in CIS. Doesn't have to be computer related, but does have to be something I like. Most tech places here require a+ certification, which I am not. Any suggestions. It's cold here, so I won't work outside, that's out of the question.<P>Any suggestions? I've gotta' register for school early Tuesday morning, and need more money for my plans for my FormulaCurrent job isn't going to cut it much longer, need to find something else, where should I look/go/try/etc?<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||87ECO5||01-02-2001||06:45 AM||||Well, it's nothing you'd want to make a career out of but I believe Lexis (no, not the car dealership) is looking for Peripheral Operators.<P>I'll get some information on it if you'd like.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||01-02-2001||08:29 AM||||The money you put into tuition and books pays off in the long run and doing it as you go along eliminates the debt after graduation. An unfortunate reality of life.  When you have the time, you don't have the money, when you have the money, you don't have the time.<P>The high paying jobs eat up all your time, so you end up farming out the "fun" things like engine swaps.<P>My nephew always wanted a high paying job so that he could party all night and sleep all day.  I'm still looking for a job like that and I'm sure that many people are.  Reality finally struck for him at 30.  Don't wait that long.||||reg||3
Z||000003||DJRice||01-02-2001||09:27 AM||||If you are a CIS major I would think that anyone looking for an "A+" certified technician could hook you up with a job.  "A+" certifications can almost be mail ordered now and it just means that you are qualified to operate a phillips screwdriver and pull the cover off of a computer.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||01-02-2001||09:28 AM||||56,<P>I just watched a show on Discovery this weekend about one of the highest paying jobs in the country... Crab Fishing.  They claim to make more in 6 months than most make in 3 years.  The first (of many) drawbacks is that you have to work out of Alaska.  :~)<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000005||GeeDee86GT||01-02-2001||10:42 AM||||F56:  Get the education. You are doing it the right way and trying to stay debt free doing it. You may need to move to get that job you want.  In Canada you can walk into a job with almost any computer training at all.  The same is probably true in different parts of the US. Besides it never gets cold here and we drive our Fieros on smooth wide roads 24/7...not<BR>Gary||||reg||12
Z||000006||fiero56||01-22-2001||01:30 PM||||I'm still on the lookout and open to suggestions on where to look at working. I am not very good at thinking up what to do. My current job, like I was expecting, isn't cutting it anymore. I've been averaging 1 day/week working for the last three weeks or so. I need to come up with some ideas before I go broke. This also delays my 3.4 project again.<BR>I would like to find something I can live off of, so I don't get stuck moving out to Oregon. If I don't come up with something I can survive off, I'm stuck heading out west, and I prefer SCC over the alternatives.||||reg||1
Z||000007||p4n1c||01-22-2001||02:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GeeDee86GT:<BR><B>In Canada you can walk into a job with almost any computer training at all.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wish I could agree with you on that.  I have extensive computer training and experience(If you think I have a swollen ego  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> , I have one person on here that can vouch for me), but was getting screwed for jobs left, right and center.  <P>The only reason I got this job with AT&T Canada is because my mom knew the senior manager from volunteer work, from what I hear it's easier down in Silicon Valley and other technical sections of the States to get eatten up by one of the big companies if you have computer experience, college diploma or not(I don't have mine, failed calculus).<P>The way to get a job in the computer industry or probably most any technical industry is with the network of people you have.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
